{\plain {We have seen that the DTFT is the
 appropriate frequency response characterization
 of FIR filters in applications involving
 indefinitely long input sequences. It is
 the commonly used frequency response and
 the object of most design methods.}}
}
.TXT 8 0 1 0
Cg a62.250000,62.125000,399
{\rtf1\ansi \deff0
{\fonttbl
{\f0\fnil Arial;}
{\f1\fnil Symbol;}
{\f2\fnil CG Times;}
}
{\plain {The DTFT has a number of additional
 properties, many of which are analogous
 to the properties of the DFT. They are 
modified in form as the IDFT is an integral
 instead of a finite sum. The proofs of 
these Properties are quite similar to the
 proofs of the DFT Properties. E.g., the
 "delta sequence" nature of I}{\fs16 \dn8 
m,n}{ of }{\ulnone \b0 (}{\ul \b 6.10}{\b0 
\ulnone )}{ is used in place of the }}
}
.ATT
.STATUS Go To Section 6, p. 7
.GOTO 6_bk.mcd
.ATT_END
