{\plain {\b \ulnone \f0 Exercise 7.1}{\f0 
\b0   Let HR(}{\f1 \b0 w}{\f0 \b0 ) and 
HI(}{\f1 \b0 w}{\f0 \b0 ) be, respectively,
 the real and imaginary parts of  H1(}{\f1 
\b0 w}{\f0 \b0 ). Then they are, respectively,
 even and odd functions which are expressible
     as HR(2}{\f1 \b0 p}{\f0 \b0 -}{\f1 
\b0 w}{\f0 \b0 ) = HR(}{\f1 \b0 w}{\f0 \b0 
) and HI(2}{\f1 \b0 p}{\f0 \b0 -}{\f1 \b0 
w}{\f0 \b0 ) = -HI(}{\f1 \b0 w}{\f0 \b0 
)}{\f0 \b0 .  }{\f0  }}
}
