{\plain {A}{ finite length sequence \{h}{\fs16 
\dn8 m}{, m=0,...,M-1\} can always be zero
 padded to an arbitrarily long length. We
 denote such a sequence \{he}{\fs16 \dn8 
n}{, n}{=0,1,...\}. Then, f}{or any nonnegative,
 finite integer n}{\fs16 \dn8 d}{, the }{\b 
\i0 translated sequence}{ }{\{hed}{\fs16 
\dn8 n}{=he}{\fs16 \dn8 n-nd}{, }{n=0,1,...\}}{
 is well defined, }{\ulnone provided he}{\ulnone 
\fs16 \dn8 n-nd}{\ulnone  is set to 0 when
 n-nd is negative}{. }{The next Property
 follows easily from the }{DTFT}{ definition
 with a simple change of summing index.}}
}
.TXT 15 0 295 0
Cg a61.250000,60.875000,259
{\rtf1\ansi \deff0
