.TXT 14 0 270 0
Cg a60.875000,61.875000,616
{\rtf1\ansi \deff0
{\fonttbl
{\f0\fnil Arial;}
{\f1\fnil Symbol;}
{\f2\fnil CG Times;}
}
{\plain {To retrace the above discussion
 of truncation, particularly Example 7.1,
 the ideal, infinitely long sequence x}{\fs16 
\dn6 n}{ would be composed of two cosine
 waves whose DTFT is given in terms of }{\f1 
d}{-functions. As these DTFTs are not functions,
 they do not have graphs as do functions.
 It is conventional to draw a vertical arrow
 at the frequencies where the }{\f1 d}{-functions
 sift. We can imply this information in 
the DFT for N-length sequences by choosing
 the very long sequence to have an integer
 number of cycles for the cosine components.
 This is a suggestive practice we follow
 when possible.}}
}
