{\plain {In this project we anticipate the
 discussion of the next two sections. }{Consider
 an FIR \{h}{\fs16 \dn6 m}{, m=0,...M\} 
of length M+1 with M even. Temporarily define
 the sequence \{g}{\fs16 \dn6 m}{=h}{\fs16 
\dn6 m-M/2}{, m=-M/2,...,M/2\}. For \{g}{\fs16 
\dn6 m}{\} (i) even, (ii) odd, and (iii)
 neither even or odd, compute the FR of 
the corresponding FIRs \{h}{\fs16 \dn6 m}{\}
 using the DFT to sample the DTFT and plot
 the magnitude and phase. Comment especially
 upon the nature of the phase.\par (You 
should use the phase-unwrapping algorithm
 (}{\ul \b Sec. 3}{) for clarity.) }{For
 each of the FIRs you considered, write 
down the ZT and plot its poles and zeros.
 Comment especially upon the nature of the
 zeros.}}
}
